  {
   "id": "w_koKvUBiywJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-02-27T20:46:12Z",
   "subject": "CRAN update",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">CRAN only required minor changes for rstan, so we should be able to take care of that very soon.<br><br>One of the issues was that g++-4.9 emits<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">warning</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;long long&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extension </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[-</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Wc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span></div></code></div><br>due to #including <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">goodrich@T540p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/opt/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan$ git grep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;long long&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cat<br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">agrad</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">160</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">unsigned</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">agrad</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">170</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">io</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">dump</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">76</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">void</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> write_val</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">const</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">unsigned</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">io</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">dump</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">92</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">void</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> write_val</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">const</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br>Why are these long long if we are not using C++11 yet? I could change these in the StanHeaders R package without us having to release a new version of Stan, but I wanted to make sure that the long longs were not essential. If they are, then rstan can be compiled in C++11 mode, but then we would not be able to build a binary with the llvm-g++-4.2 compiler on older versions of the Mac operating system.<br><br>Ben<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "xsNstmsnMSwJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-02-28T03:41:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: CRAN update",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Bob, what&#39;s up with this long long stuff?</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, February 27, 2015 at 3:46:12 PM UTC-5, Ben Goodrich wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">CRAN only required minor changes for rstan, so we should be able to take care of that very soon.<br><br>One of the issues was that g++-4.9 emits<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">warning</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;long long&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extension </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[-</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Wc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span></div></code></div><br>due to #including <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">goodrich@T540p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/opt/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan$ git grep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;long long&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cat<br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">agrad</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">160</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">unsigned</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">agrad</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">170</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">io</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">dump</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">76</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">void</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> write_val</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">const</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">unsigned</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">io</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#008\">dump</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">92</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">void</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> write_val</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">const</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br>Why are these long long if we are not using C++11 yet? I could change these in the StanHeaders R package without us having to release a new version of Stan, but I wanted to make sure that the long longs were not essential. If they are, then rstan can be compiled in C++11 mode, but then we would not be able to build a binary with the llvm-g++-4.2 compiler on older versions of the Mac operating system.<br><br>Ben<br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "GRwJTUkRVokJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2015-02-28T03:56:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] Re: CRAN update",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I filed an issue:\r<br>\r<br>  <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1316\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1316&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473739218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2DA0Fj1D48ZNT9WwyKLfxT\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1316</a>\r<br>\r<br>I&#39;m about to go fix it now.  Shouldn&#39;t take long at all.\r<br>\r<br>I believe we put it in to deal with 64-bit Windows compilers,\r<br>which treat &quot;size_t&quot; as synonymous with &quot;unsigned long long&quot;, rather\r<br>than &quot;unsigned long&quot; like the Unices (Linux/Mac).  We can&#39;t have\r<br>both &quot;size_t&quot; and &quot;unsigned long&quot; due to ambiguity, and we didn&#39;t \r<br>know how to work around it before.  \r<br>\r<br>We&#39;re better at C++ now, and I think I can just use Boost&#39;s enable_if \r<br>mechanism to restrict to primitives without running afoul of\r<br>Windows issues.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Feb 28, 2015, at 2:41 PM, Ben Goodrich &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Bob, what&#39;s up with this long long stuff?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Friday, February 27, 2015 at 3:46:12 PM UTC-5, Ben Goodrich wrote:\r<br>&gt; CRAN only required minor changes for rstan, so we should be able to take care of that very soon.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; One of the issues was that g++-4.9 emits\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; warning: &#39;long long&#39; is a C++11 extension [-Wc++11-long-long]\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; due to #including \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; goodrich@T540p:/opt/stan$ git grep -F -n &quot;long long&quot; src/stan | cat\r<br>&gt; src/stan/agrad/rev/var.hpp:160:      var(unsigned long long n) :\r<br>&gt; src/stan/agrad/rev/var.hpp:170:      var(long long n) :\r<br>&gt; src/stan/io/dump.hpp:76:      void write_val(const unsigned long long int&amp; n) {\r<br>&gt; src/stan/io/dump.hpp:92:      void write_val(const long long&amp; n) {\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Why are these long long if we are not using C++11 yet? I could change these in the StanHeaders R package without us having to release a new version of Stan, but I wanted to make sure that the long longs were not essential. If they are, then rstan can be compiled in C++11 mode, but then we would not be able to build a binary with the llvm-g++-4.2 compiler on older versions of the Mac operating system.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Ben\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; -- \r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;stan development mailing list&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-dev+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473739218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3d-1c4YpCSCFp3mDr7oKYa\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
